- Subtask `4.3 / 9`:\n181:   - decide how `manual_obligatory` and `manual_multiplicity` become required,\n182:     optional, or repeated domain fields\n183: - Subtask `4.4 / 9`:\n184:   - document impacts from known structural limitations such as `xs:choice`,\n185:     weak `minOccurs` enforcement, and attributes typed as `object`\n186: \n187: ### Step `5 / 9` - Define Policy Per Semantic Reference Kind\n188: \n189: - Step summary:\n190:   - define the core semantic treatment for each normalized\n191:     `SemanticReferenceKind`\n192: - Step type:\n193:   - semantic design\n194: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n195:   - one or more new hand-maintained semantic-policy modules under\n196:     `src/cvn_codegen/`\n197:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`\n198: - Root task `5 / 9`:\n199:   - define open-versus-closed treatment and semantic shape by normalized\n200:     reference kind\n201: - Subtask `5.1 / 9`:\n202:   - compact enum-like table\n203: - Subtask `5.2 / 9`:\n204:   - compact scale or measure table\n205: - Subtask `5.3 / 9`:\n206:   - identifier-type table\n207: - Subtask `5.4 / 9`:\n208:   - scope table\n209: - Subtask `5.5 / 9`:\n210:   - subtype-backed controlled family\n211: - Subtask `5.6 / 9`:\n212:   - hierarchical thematic classification\n213: - Subtask `5.7 / 9`:\n214:   - side-package registry\n215: - Subtask `5.8 / 9`:\n216:   - side-package thesaurus or vocabulary\n217: - Subtask `5.9 / 9`:\n218:   - unresolved manual-only reference\n219: - Subtask `5.10 / 9`:\n220:   - technically present but under-traced table\n221: \n222: ### Step `6 / 9` - Define Naming And Traceability Rules\n223: \n224: - Step summary:\n225:   - define how domain-facing names are derived while preserving CVN code and\n226:     XML traceability\n227: - Step type:\n228:   - standards and technical design\n229: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n230:   - one or more new hand-maintained semantic-policy modules under\n231:     `src/cvn_codegen/`\n232:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`\n233: - Root task `6 / 9`:\n234:   - define naming rules for future domain classes, fields, and modules\n235: - Subtask `6.1 / 9`:\n236:   - decide the naming-language policy, including the role of Spanish academic\n237:     terminology\n238: - Subtask `6.2 / 9`:\n239:   - decide how multilingual manual labels are normalized into stable\n240:     identifiers\n241: - Subtask `6.3 / 9`:\n242:   - define collision-resolution rules for repeated or technically noisy names\n243: - Subtask `6.4 / 9`:\n244:   - define how semantic outputs preserve traceability back to CVN `code` and\n245:     `xml_path`\n246: \n247: ### Step `7 / 9` - Design Override Mechanism\n248: \n249: - Step summary:\n250:   - design explicit override support for cases that generic semantic rules\n251:     cannot resolve safely\n252: - Step type:\n253:   - contract definition and technical design\n254: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n255:   - one or more new hand-maintained override modules under `src/cvn_codegen/`\n256:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`\n257: - Root task `7 / 9`:\n258:   - define override granularity, structure, and precedence\n259: - Subtask `7.1 / 9`:\n260:   - decide whether overrides can target CVN `code`\n261: - Subtask `7.2 / 9`:\n262:   - decide whether overrides can target `xml_path`\n263: - Subtask `7.3 / 9`:\n264:   - decide whether overrides can target `reference_resolution.semantic_kind`\n265: - Subtask `7.4 / 9`:\n266:   - decide whether overrides can target serialization pattern\n267: - Subtask `7.5 / 9`:\n268:   - define precedence rules when multiple generic or specific rules collide\n269: \n270: ### Step `8 / 9` - Validate Policy Against Real Cases\n271: \n272: - Step summary:\n273:   - verify that the semantic policy can classify and explain representative real\n274:     cases without reopening unresolved semantic design work in issue `#15`\n275: - Step type:\n276:   - validation, documentation, and possible contract-level test preparation\n277: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n278:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`\n279:   - `docs/pipeline/known_limitations.md` if a new limitation is discovered\n280:   - optional semantic-policy tests if validation is captured in executable form\n281: - Root task `8 / 9`:\n282:   - validate the policy against representative normalized examples\n283: - Subtask `8.1 / 9`:\n284:   - validate a simple scalar field\n285: - Subtask `8.2 / 9`:\n286:   - validate a compact closed controlled table\n287: - Subtask `8.3 / 9`:\n288:   - validate a compact open controlled table\n289: - Subtask `8.4 / 9`:\n290:   - validate registry, thesaurus, and hierarchical references\n291: - Subtask `8.5 / 9`:\n292:   - validate a subtype-backed controlled family\n293: - Subtask `8.6 / 9`:\n294:   - validate unresolved and under-traced references\n295: - Subtask `8.7 / 9`:\n296:   - validate wrapper, `choice`, recursion, and override cases\n297: \n298: ### Step `9 / 9` - Document Final Policy And Prepare Handoff\n299: \n300: - Step summary:\n301:   - record final semantic-policy decisions, unresolved limits, and the handoff\n302:     contract that issue `#15` will consume\n303: - Step type:\n304:   - documentation and issue closure preparation\n305: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n306:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`\n307:   - `docs/context/current_status.md`\n308:   - `docs/roadmap/cvn_generation_roadmap.md`\n309:   - `docs/pipeline/known_limitations.md` if new limitations are found\n310: - Root task `9 / 9`:\n311:   - document the final policy and prepare the downstream handoff to issue `#15`\n312: - Subtask `9.1 / 9`:\n313:   - record any deviations from the original issue plan\n314: - Subtask `9.2 / 9`:\n315:   - leave a clear downstream checklist for issue `#15`\n316: - Subtask `9.3 / 9`:\n317:   - update roadmap and context documents when issue state changes\n318: >>>>>>> Stashed changes\n319: \n320: ## Established Semantic Policy Plan\n321: \n322: The issue `#14` planning session established the decisions below. These\n323: decisions are the operative specification for implementation work.\n324: \n325: ### Scope Boundary\n326: \n327: Issue `#14` consumes only typed normalized metadata from issue `#13` as policy\n328: inputs. Raw XML, raw XSD, and generated structural classes may be inspected for\n329: human validation or override evidence, but they must not become base semantic\n330: inputs.\n331: \n332: Required normalized inputs are:\n333: \n334: - `code`\n335: - `xml_path`\n336: - `manual_type`\n337: - `manual_multiplicity`\n338: - `manual_obligatory`\n339: - `reference_resolution.status`\n340: - `reference_resolution.source_family`\n341: - `reference_resolution.source_artifact`\n342: - `reference_resolution.resolved_name`\n343: - `reference_resolution.serialization_pattern`\n344: - `reference_resolution.semantic_kind`\n345: - `reference_resolution.trace`\n346: \n347: Issue `#14` must not reimplement source-family detection, serialization-pattern\n348: classification, semantic-kind classification, side-package detection,\n349: subtype-backed detection, unresolved-reference detection, under-traced-table\n350: detection, manual/tree overlap computation, or `xml_path` construction.\n351: \n352: If a repeated semantic decision needs raw source inspection, the missing data\n353: belongs in issue `#13`. If the need is isolated and not generalizable, issue\n354: `#14` may express it as an explicit override with trace evidence.\n355: \n356: ### Contract Families\n357: \n358: The semantic policy contract should be implemented as explicit typed Python\n359: structures, using `dataclass` records and `Enum` values. The root contract should\n360: be an indexed `SemanticPolicyBundle`.\n361: \n362: Minimum contract families are:\n363: \n364: - `SemanticPolicyBundle`\n365: - `SemanticFieldPolicy`\n366: - `ReferenceKindPolicy`\n367: - `BaseTypePolicy`\n368: - `NamingPolicy`\n369: - `MultiplicityPolicy`\n370: - `ChoiceWrapperPolicy`\n371: - `OverrideRule`\n372: - `ValidationCaseDefinition`\n373: - `PolicyMetadata`\n374: - `SemanticDecisionTrace`\n375: \n376: The bundle should expose deterministic lookups by CVN `code`, `xml_path`,\n377: `reference_resolution.semantic_kind`, `reference_resolution.serialization_pattern`,\n378: `manual_type`, and wrapper family.\n379: \n380: ### Policy Enums\n381: \n382: The semantic contract should define these policy categories:\n383: \n384: | Category | Values |\n385: | --- | --- |\n386: | `SemanticBaseKind` | `TEXT`, `CONTROLLED_REFERENCE`, `DATE_LIKE`, `DECIMAL_NUMBER`, `BOOLEAN`, `DURATION_LIKE`, `UNKNOWN` |\n387: | `WrapperPolicyKind` | `COLLAPSE`, `VALUE_OBJECT_CANDIDATE`, `CHOICE_OBJECT_CANDIDATE`, `PRESERVE_STRUCTURAL_TRACE` |\n388: | `PresenceKind` | `REQUIRED`, `OPTIONAL`, `UNKNOWN` |\n389: | `CardinalityKind` | `SINGLE`, `REPEATED`, `UNKNOWN` |\n390: | `StructuralLimitationFlag` | `CHOICE_NOT_ENFORCED`, `LIST_MIN_OCCURS_WEAK`, `OBJECT_TYPED_ATTRIBUTE`, `WRAPPER_ERGONOMICS` |\n391: | `DomainShapeKind` | `PLAIN_VALUE`, `STRICT_ENUM_CANDIDATE`, `OPEN_CODED_VALUE`, `MEASURE_OR_SCALE_VALUE`, `IDENTIFIER_REFERENCE`, `SCOPE_REFERENCE`, `SUBTYPE_BACKED_VALUE`, `HIERARCHICAL_CODE_REFERENCE`, `REGISTRY_REFERENCE`, `VOCABULARY_REFERENCE`, `UNRESOLVED_REFERENCE`, `UNDER_TRACED_REFERENCE` |\n392: | `PolicyConfidence` | `HIGH`, `MEDIUM`, `LOW`, `REQUIRES_REVIEW` |\n393: | `EnumEligibility` | `ELIGIBLE`, `INELIGIBLE`, `REVIEW_REQUIRED` |\n394: \n395: ### Lookup And Override Precedence\n396: \n397: Semantic policy resolution must use this precedence order:\n398: \n399: 1. `code + xml_path` override\n400: 2. `code` override\n401: 3. `xml_path` override\n402: 4. `reference_resolution.semantic_kind` policy or override\n403: 5. `reference_resolution.serialization_pattern` refinement\n404: 6. `manual_type` base policy\n405: 7. wrapper policy\n406: 8. presence/cardinality policy\n407: 9. global defaults\n408: \n409: Overrides may change only semantic-policy outputs such as `domain_shape_kind`,\n410: `fallback_shape_kind`, `enum_eligibility`, `policy_confidence`,\n411: `wrapper_policy`, `presence_kind`, `cardinality_kind`, `normalized_name`,\n412: `naming_confidence`, `structural_limitation_flags`, notes, and diagnostics.\n413: \n414: Overrides must not mutate normalized input facts such as `code`, `xml_path`,\n415: `manual_type`, `manual_reference_table`, `reference_resolution.status`,\n416: `reference_resolution.source_family`, `reference_resolution.semantic_kind`,\n417: `reference_resolution.serialization_pattern`, or upstream trace facts.\n418: \n419: Same-priority conflicts should produce `PolicyConfidence.REQUIRES_REVIEW` rather\n420: than silently choosing one rule.\n421: \n422: ### Base Type Policy\n423: \n424: Issue `#14` defines semantic base kinds, not final Python/domain output types.\n425: Issue `#15` will map these semantic kinds to concrete generated Python artifacts.\n426: \n427: | `manual_type` condition | Semantic base kind |\n428: | --- | --- |\n429: | `Alphanumeric` without resolved controlled reference | `TEXT` |\n430: | `Alphanumeric` with `reference_resolution.semantic_kind` | `CONTROLLED_REFERENCE` |\n431: | `Date` | `DATE_LIKE` |\n432: | `Double` | `DECIMAL_NUMBER` |\n433: | `Boolean` | `BOOLEAN` |\n434: | `Duration` | `DURATION_LIKE` |\n435: | missing or unknown manual type | `UNKNOWN` |\n436: \n437: Wrappers should collapse only when they add no domain information and do not\n438: represent meaningful `xs:choice`, variable granularity, or structural\n439: traceability concerns. `FlexibleDatesType`, `OfficialIdType`, `EntityTypeType`,\n440: and `EntityNameType` must be marked as `CHOICE_OBJECT_CANDIDATE`.\n441: \n442: ### Presence And Cardinality Policy\n443: \n444: | Normalized field | Value | Policy output |\n445: | --- | --- | --- |\n446: | `manual_obligatory` | `True` | `PresenceKind.REQUIRED` |\n447: