          "text": "<path>/mnt/e/Carlos/unii/tfg/repo/TFG-open-cvn-schema/PROJECT_GUIDE.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Project Guide\n2: \n3: ## Purpose\n4: \n5: This file is the human entry point for understanding the repository.\n6: It summarizes the project purpose, the current implementation focus, the\n7: documentation structure, and the repository rules that matter to contributors\n8: and maintainers.\n9: \n10: ## What This Repository Is\n11: \n12: This repository contains a Trabajo de Fin de Grado focused on defining an open\n13: data schema for representing academic and research CVs in Spain, taking the\n14: CVN format as the starting point.\n15: \n16: The long-term goal is not only to mirror the official CVN package, but to make\n17: curriculum data easier to validate, transform, store, and export through open\n18: tooling.\n19: \n20: ## Current Technical Scope\n21: \n22: The repository is currently centered on the generation pipeline that turns the\n23: official CVN XML/XSD package into reproducible Python artifacts.\n24: \n25: Current and planned layers are:\n26: \n27: 1. structural bindings generated from the official CVN XML/XSD package\n28: 2. normalized metadata extracted from the official supporting XML documents\n29: 3. semantic mapping rules that recover domain meaning from the structural layer\n30: 4. domain-oriented Pydantic models built over normalized metadata\n31: \n32: This means the repository is currently implementing the technical foundation\n33: for the future parser, validator, JSON-oriented schema, and downstream export\n34: work. It is not yet the full end-user CV tooling envisioned by the TFG.\n35: \n36: ## Recommended Reading Order For Humans\n37: \n38: When you need to understand the project state before making changes, read these\n39: files in order:\n40: \n41: 1. `PROJECT_GUIDE.md`\n42: 2. `docs/context/project_context_index.md`\n43: 3. `docs/context/current_status.md`\n44: 4. the relevant issue document under `docs/roadmap/issues/`\n45: 5. supporting architecture or limitation documents linked from that issue\n46: \n47: ## Repository Rules And Conventions\n48: \n49: - Treat `docs/CvnXML_v1.4.3_2.1_17012025/` as the canonical source package for\n50:   the CVN generation roadmap\n51: - Do not edit `src/generated/` manually\n52: - Keep hand-maintained pipeline logic in `src/cvn_codegen/`\n53: - Keep future semantic or domain models in `src/models/cvn/`\n54: - Follow issue order unless there is a deliberate reason to work out of order\n55: - Record implementation deviations from the original issue plan in the issue\n56:   document for that issue\n57: - Update persistent documentation in the same session as the code change\n58: \n59: ## Documentation Map\n60: \n61: ### Entry Points\n62: \n63: - `README.md`: high-level repository overview\n64: - `PROJECT_GUIDE.md`: human-oriented project entry point\n65: - `AGENTS.md`: operational rules and document map for agents\n66: - `CONTRIBUTING.md`: contributor onboarding and documentation obligations\n67: \n68: ### Current State And Context\n69: \n70: - `docs/context/project_context_index.md`: documentation index and reading map\n71: - `docs/context/current_status.md`: latest implementation state and next steps\n72: \n73: ### Architecture And Limits\n74: \n75: - `docs/pipeline/cvn_pydantic_generation_pipeline.md`: architecture of the CVN\n76:   generation workflow\n77: - `docs/pipeline/known_limitations.md`: structural limitations, source-package\n78:   inconsistencies, and follow-up implications\n79: - `docs/adr/`: architecture decision records\n80: \n81: ### Roadmap And Issue History\n82: \n83: - `docs/roadmap/cvn_generation_roadmap.md`: roadmap from issue `#8` through\n84:   issue `#17`\n85: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-08-epic-cvn-automation.md`: epic summary and\n86:   checkpoints\n87: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-11-project-infrastructure.md`: authoritative\n88:   record of issue `#11`\n89: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-12-structural-bindings.md`: authoritative record\n90:   of issue `#12`\n91: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-13-normalization.md`: authoritative record of issue\n92:   `#13`\n93: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-semantic-mapping-rules.md`: planned scope of\n94:   issue `#14`\n95: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-15-domain-model-generator.md`: planned scope of\n96:   issue `#15`\n97: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-16-generation-pipeline-tests.md`: planned scope of\n98:   issue `#16`\n99: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-17-workflow-documentation.md`: planned scope of\n100:   issue `#17`\n101: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-25-github-actions-ci-pipeline-for-pr-testing-on-main-and-development.md`:\n102:   authoritative record of issue `#25`\n103: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-1-runner-logging-convention.md`: maintenance\n104:   record for the runner logging convention update\n105: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-2-human-project-entrypoint.md`: maintenance\n106:   record for the human project entry point and documentation update protocol\n107:   alignment\n108: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-3-cvn-source-package-documentation-expansion.md`:\n109:   maintenance record for the source-package documentation expansion and\n110:   consistency cleanup\n111: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-4-structural-scope-correction-for-auxiliary-source-package-artifacts.md`:\n112:   corrective plan for extending issues `#11` and `#12` to the auxiliary source\n113:   package families\n114: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-5-normalization-resolution-layer-for-auxiliary-reference-sources.md`:\n115:   corrective plan for extending issue `#13` with auxiliary-reference resolution\n116: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-6-roadmap-realignment-for-auxiliary-catalog-semantic-integration.md`:\n117:   corrective plan for replanning issues `#8`, `#14` to `#17`, and the CI impact\n118:   from the auxiliary catalog integration\n119: \n120: ### Development Reference\n121: \n122: - `docs/development/setup.md`: environment and execution commands\n123: - `docs/development/code_style.md`: code style, typing, and conventions\n124: - `docs/documentation/documentation_conventions.md`: documentation taxonomy,\n125:   cross-linking rules, and update protocol\n126: \n127: ### Source Package Analysis\n128: \n129: - `docs/informe_estructura_cvnxml_v1.4.3.md`: detailed analysis of the core CVN\n130:   package structure and usage\n131: - `docs/cvn_source_package_auxiliary_artifacts.md`: detailed explanation of the\n132:   auxiliary `Entity`, `ReferenceTables/Subtypes`, and `Thesaurus` families\n133: - `docs/cvn_source_package_annex_table_coverage.md`: practical mapping of Annex\n134:   I tables to core XSDs, side packages, and unresolved manual-only cases\n135: - `docs/cvn_annex_priority_table_families.md`: detailed reference for the\n136:   high-impact Annex I table families most relevant to semantic mapping work\n137: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch3.md`: detailed reference for the next\n138:   group of Annex I families covering participation, summons, programme,\n139:   publication, support, and event tables\n140: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch4.md`: detailed reference for the next\n141:   group of Annex I families covering activity, management, scope, language,\n142:   time, qualification, access, and evaluation tables\n143: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch5.md`: detailed reference for the next\n144:   group of Annex I families covering subject, stay, dedication, duration,\n145:   formation, teaching, prizes, and thematic tables\n146: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch6.md`: detailed reference for the next\n147:   group of Annex I families covering region, province, sex, and situation\n148:   tables\n149: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch7.md`: detailed reference for the next\n150:   group of Annex I families covering agency, collaboration, and cooperation\n151:   tables, including unresolved `CVN_AGENCY_C`\n152: - `docs/cvn_annex_table_families_batch8.md`: detailed reference for