begins from only raw normalized manual and tree metadata.\n51: It must start from the validated enriched normalization output implemented in\n52: issue `#13` after hotfix `#5`, with auxiliary structural visibility already in\n53: place from hotfix `#4`.\n54: \n55: The corrected semantic-policy input now includes at minimum:\n56: \n57: - `manual_type`\n58: - `manual_multiplicity`\n59: - `manual_obligatory`\n60: - `xml_path`\n61: - `reference_resolution.status`\n62: - `reference_resolution.source_family`\n63: - `reference_resolution.source_artifact`\n64: - `reference_resolution.serialization_pattern`\n65: - `reference_resolution.semantic_kind`\n66: - `reference_resolution.trace`\n67: \n68: Issue `#14` must consume that typed metadata. It must not rebuild source-family,\n69: side-package, subtype-backed, or hierarchical-reference detection from prose\n70: documents or ad hoc table-name inspection.\n71: \n72: >>>>>>> Stashed changes\n73: ## Planned Execution Steps\n74: \n75: The implementation of issue `#14` should begin from the enriched normalization\n76: layer produced in issue `#13` and should leave issue `#15` with an explicit,\n77: <<<<<<< Updated upstream\n78: deterministic semantic policy to consume.\n79: =======\n80: deterministic semantic policy to consume without reopening source-discovery\n81: questions.\n82: \n83: ## Agreed Execution Plan\n84: \n85: The following plan was agreed before starting implementation work on issue\n86: `#14`. It is the operative execution sequence for the issue and should guide the\n87: step-by-step development session.\n88: \n89: ### Step `1 / 9` - Define Exact Scope Boundary\n90: \n91: - Step summary:\n92:   - define the exact execution boundary of issue `#14` so semantic policy,\n93:     normalization responsibilities, and generator responsibilities stay clearly\n94:     separated\n95: - Step type:\n96:   - standards, contracts, and documentation\n97: - Files to modify or add if needed:\n98:   - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-14-sem