            "output": "<path>/mnt/e/Carlos/unii/tfg/repo/TFG-open-cvn-schema/docs/pipeline/known_limitations.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Known Limitations\n2: \n3: ## Purpose\n4: \n5: This document records known limitations of the current pipeline so later issues\n6: do not need to rediscover them.\n7: \n8: ## Structural Binding Limitations\n9: \n10: ### `xs:choice` Is Not Enforced As Mutual Exclusivity\n11: \n12: - Affected areas include:\n13:   - `FlexibleDatesType`\n14:   - `OfficialIdType`\n15:   - `EntityTypeType`\n16:   - `EntityNameType`\n17: - Impact:\n18:   - generated Pydantic models may accept states that are invalid with respect to\n19:     the source XSD\n20: - Expected follow-up:\n21:   - issue `#14` should define policy\n22:   - issue `#15` should restore domain-facing semantics\n23: \n24: ### `minOccurs` Is Not Enforced For Generated Lists\n25: \n26: - Generated list fields with `default_factory=list` do not enforce the minimum\n27:   cardinality implied by the XSD\n28: - Impact:\n29:   - empty lists may be accepted in object construction even when the XSD\n30:     expects at least one element\n31: - Expected follow-up:\n32:   - issue `#14` and issue `#15`\n33: \n34: ### Some Attributes Are Typed As `object`\n35: \n36: - Seen in parts of `specification_manual` and `tree_model`\n37: - Impact:\n38:   - validation is weaker than the XSD suggests\n39:   - ergonomics are worse for downstream code\n40: - Expected follow-up:\n41:   - issue `#14` and issue `#15`\n42: \n43: ### XML Helper Types Are Less Ergonomic Than Primitives\n44: \n45: - Wrappers such as `CVN_duration`, `CVN_gYear`, and `CVN_gYearMonth` map to XML\n46:   helper types such as `XmlDuration` and `XmlPeriod`\n47: - Impact:\n48:   - structural fidelity is preserved, but programmatic usage is more delicate\n49: - Expected follow-up:\n50:   - issue `#14` and issue `#15`\n51: \n52: ## Generation Process Limitations\n53: \n54: ### `tree_model` Needs A Target-Specific xsdata Override\n55: \n56: - Default structural generation hit circular dependency problems\n57: - Current workaround:\n58:   - `--unnest-classes`\n59: - Impact:\n60:   - generation is reproducible, but not uniform across all three targets\n61: - Expected follow-up:\n62:   - keep documented through issue `#17`\n63: \n64: ## Canonical Source Package Inconsistencies\n65: \n66: ### `CVNTreeModel.xml` Diverges From `CVNTreeModel_v1.0.xsd`\n67: \n68: - Confirmed discrepancy:\n69:   - the XML includes `<Type>` inside `Indicator`\n70:   - the XSD only declares `Value` and `Child` inside `Indicator`\n71: - Confirmed scope of the discrepancy:\n72:   - the canonical XML contains `438` `Indicator` nodes with\n73:     `mo:name=\"Type\"`, which is compatible with the documented tree-model\n74:     structure\n75:   - only `2` real child elements named `<Type>` were found in the canonical XML\n76:   - those `2` unexpected child elements appear under:\n77:     - `Indicator mo:name=\"Type\" mo:code=\"060.030.070.220\"`\n78:     - `Indicator mo:name=\"Type\" mo:code=\"060.030.070.230\"`\n79:   - both unexpected child elements contain the value:\n80:     `CVN_QualityTypeType@AuxTable.xsd`\n81: - Comparison with the tree-model documentation:\n82:   - `TreeModel_v1.0 20090331 v1.0.pdf` defines `Indicator` children as only\n83:     `Value` and `Child`\n84:   - the document does not describe `<Type>` as an allowed child element of\n85:     `Indicator`\n86:   - this makes the two `<Type>` elements a source inconsistency, not a\n87:     documented feature of the tree model\n88: - Practical consequence:\n89:   - the generated `tree_model` binding is correct with respect to the XSD, but\n90:     cannot fully parse the canonical XML file\n91: - Normalization consequence:\n92:   - issue `#13` should treat `xml_path` as a structural path built from\n93:     `CVNTreeModel`, `Node`, `CVNItem`, `Property`, and `Indicator`\n94:   - the unexpected `<Type>` child elements should be recorded as explicit\n95:     mismatches or special-case findings, not folded into the standard structural\n96:     path model\n97: - Parse status:\n98:   - `SpecificationManual.xml`: parse OK\n99:   - `CVNTreeModel.xml`: parse blocked by XML/XSD mismatch\n100: - Expected follow-up:\n101:   - issue `#13` must treat the tree-model XML as a source of truth for\n102:     normalization even when the XSD does not describe it completely\n103: \n104: ### Auxiliary Catalog Families Preserve Historical Packaging Drift\n105: \n106: - affected families:\n107:   - `Entity`\n108:   - `ReferenceTables/Subtypes`\n109:   - `Thesaurus`\n110: - confirmed issues:\n111:   - XML `schemaLocation` values assume colocated XSD files, while the preserved\n112:     repository package stores XML and XSD in separate directories\n113:   - several `Leeme*.txt` files mention filenames that do not exactly match the\n114:     preserved repository filenames, such as `Subtypes.xml` instead of\n115:     `Subtype_Spa.xml`, or lowercase thesaurus filenames that differ from the\n116:     actual files\n117:   - side families duplicate ISO helper schemas instead of using one fully shared\n118:     physical artifact\n119:   - `Subtypes` materials preserve version drift between PDF, XSD, and XML files\n120: - impact:\n121:   - package exploration and automated file resolution cannot rely on filenames or\n122:     relative schema locations alone\n123:   - tooling must resolve these families through repository-aware path mapping and\n124:     documented semantic relationships\n125: - expected follow-up:\n126:   - issue `#14` should define semantic policy for side-package references\n127:   - issue `#15` should decide which of these auxiliary artifacts become domain\n128:     sources versus support registries\n129: \n130: ### Some Annex-I Table References Remain Unresolved From The Package Alone\n131: \n132: - confirmed example:\n133:   - `CVN_AGENCY_C` appears referenced from the manual material but does not map\n134:     cleanly to a matching table in `ReferenceTables.xml`\n135: - impact:\n136:   - not every table name from the manual can yet be promoted to a strict\n137:     machine-resolved enum or closed catalog using the source package alone\n138: - expected follow-up:\n139:   - issue `#14` should define open versus closed treatment for unresolved tables\n140:   - issue `#15` should preserve such cases as explicit external or manual-only\n141:     references unless stronger evidence is introduced\n142: \n143: ### `Subtype_Spa.xml` Does Not Provide A Direct Table-Family Bridge\n144: \n145: - confirmed behavior:\n146:   - `Subtype_Spa.xml` can be parsed and used to prove subtype catalog\n147:     availability\n148:   - the preserved XML is keyed by numeric subtype item codes such as `001`,\n149:     `002`, and not by reference-table family names such as `CVN_KNOW_A`\n150: - impact:\n151:   - the current normalization layer can classify tables as subtype-backed and\n152:     record that subtype catalog data is available, but it does not yet verify a\n153:     strict per-table-family bridge directly from `Subtype_Spa.xml`\n154: - expected follow-up:\n155:   - issue `#14` should decide whether subtype-backed semantic policy needs a\n156:     stronger bridge than catalog availability alone\n157:   - later maintenance work may add a stricter bridge only if reliable evidence\n158:     is introduced from the preserved source package\n159: \n160: ## Documentation Rule\n161: \n162: Whenever a new limitation is discovered, add it here and reference the issue\n163: expected to address it.\n\n(End of file - total 163 lines)\n</content>",
