s added\n116:   - `SpecificationManual.xml` parse verified\n117:   - `CVNTreeModel.xml` mismatch documented\n118: \n119: Authoritative record:\n120: \n121: - `docs/roadmap/issues/issue-12-structural-bindings.md`\n122: \n123: ## Documented Maintenance Hotfixes\n124: \n125: ### Hotfix `#1`\n126: \n127: - Goal:\n128:   replace operational `print` usage in the xsdata runner with `logging` and\n129:   document the repository convention for logging and string interpolation\n130: - Scope:\n131:   - define a module logger in `src/cvn_codegen/xsdata_runner.py`\n132:   - replace runner progress and error `print` calls with the appropriate\n133:     logging level\n134:   - document that `print` is reserved for direct console interaction\n135:   - document f-strings as the project standard for interpolated strings\n136: \n137: Authoritative record:\n138: \n139: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-1-runner-logging-convention.md`\n140: \n141: ### Hotfix `#2`\n142: \n143: - Goal:\n144:   introduce `PROJECT_GUIDE.md` as the human repository entry point and align\n145:   the documentation maintenance protocol with that change\n146: - Scope:\n147:   - create a human-oriented entry point equivalent in practical guidance to\n148:     `AGENTS.md`\n149:   - stop routing human readers through `AGENTS.md` from top-level docs\n150:   - distinguish human and agent reading orders in the persistent context docs\n151:   - require updating `PROJECT_GUIDE.md` when human-facing repository guidance\n152:     changes\n153: \n154: Authoritative record:\n155: \n156: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-2-human-project-entrypoint.md`\n157: \n158: ### Hotfix `#3`\n159: \n160: - Goal:\n161:   document the canonical source package beyond the core structural subset and\n162:   preserve the auxiliary-family and Annex-I coverage analysis needed by later\n163:   issues\n164: \n165: Authoritative record:\n166: \n167: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-3-cvn-source-package-documentation-expansion.md`\n168: \n169: ### Hotfix `#4`\n170: \n171: - Goal:\n172:   correct the structural scope of issues `#11` and `#12` so the repository\n173:   infrastructure and structural generation plan cover the auxiliary source\n174:   package families\n175: \n176: Authoritative record:\n177: \n178: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-4-structural-scope-correction-for-auxiliary-source-package-artifacts.md`\n179: \n180: ### Hotfix `#5`\n181: \n182: - Goal:\n183:   correct issue `#13` so normalization grows from plain manual/tree alignment\n184:   into an additive resolution layer over auxiliary reference sources\n185: - Implemented outcome:\n186:   - normalization contract enriched with typed auxiliary-reference metadata\n187:   - normalization orchestration extended with optional auxiliary-source inputs\n188:   - deterministic resolution now covers direct tables, subtype-backed families,\n189:     side-package registries, side-package thesauri, hierarchical thematic\n190:     references, unresolved cases, and under-traced documented tables\n191: \n192: Authoritative record:\n193: \n194: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-5-normalization-resolution-layer-for-auxiliary-reference-sources.md`\n195: \n196: ### Hotfix `#6`\n197: \n198: - Goal:\n199:   realign the roadmap for issues `#8`, `#14`, `#15`, `#16`, and `#17` around\n200:   the auxiliary catalog integration now known to be required\n201: \n202: Authoritative record:\n203: \n204: - `docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-6-roadmap-realignment-for-auxiliary-catalog-semantic-integration.md`\n205: \n206: ## Future Work Focus\n207: \n208: ### Issue `#13`\n209: \n210: - Goal:\n211:   build a normalized metadata layer consumable by the future domain-model\n212:   generator\n213: - Required scope:\n214:   - parse both metadata XML sources\n215:   - build indexes keyed by CVN `code`\n216:   - extract technical XML paths from the tree model\n217:   - compare overlap and detect mismatches\n218:   - expose reusable normalized structures with source traceability\n219: \n220: ### 