e old `%`-style string formatting in repository code\n56: \n57: ## Generated Code Boundaries\n58: \n59: - `src/generated/` is generated code and must not be edited manually\n60: - semantic cleanup, overrides, normalization, and domain generation belong\n61:   outside `src/generated/`\n62: - the structural layer favors fidelity over ergonomics\n63: \n64: ## Domain-Specific Conventions\n65: \n66: - Preserve CVN code traceability throughout the pipeline\n67: - Prefer Spanish academic terminology when mirroring source semantics\n68: - Use ORCID, CERIF, and JSON-oriented naming consistently when introducing\n69:   domain-facing models later in the roadmap\n70: \n71: ## Academic Project Conventions\n72: \n73: - Keep architecture decisions documented\n74: - Record limitations explicitly rather than hiding them\n75: - Prioritize reproducibility over convenience for generation workflows\n76: - Ensure future contributors can reconstruct the pipeline from repository docs\n\n(End of file - total 76 lines)\n</content>",
