            "output": "<path>/mnt/e/Carlos/unii/tfg/repo/TFG-open-cvn-schema/docs/development/setup.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Development Setup\n2: \n3: ## Prerequisites\n4: \n5: - `uv`\n6: - Python `3.14`\n7: \n8: ## Environment Setup\n9: \n10: Pin Python if needed:\n11: \n12: ```bash\n13: uv python pin 3.14\n14: ```\n15: \n16: Create and synchronize the environment:\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: uv sync --group codegen --group testing\n20: uv pip install -e .\n21: ```\n22: \n23: The editable install is required so the `src/` layout is importable during\n24: tests and local execution.\n25: \n26: ## Dependency Groups\n27: \n28: - `codegen`: structural generation tooling, including `xsdata` and\n29:   `xsdata-pydantic`\n30: - `testing`: test dependencies, currently centered on `pytest`\n31: \n32: The project should use dependency groups whenever it is reasonably possible and\n33: useful to separate concerns. As a rule:\n34: \n35: - keep true runtime dependencies in `[project.dependencies]`\n36: - keep structural generation tooling in `[dependency-groups].codegen`\n37: - keep test-only tooling in `[dependency-groups].testing`\n38: \n39: Create a new dependency group when a set of tools is clearly non-runtime and has\n40: its own execution context, maintenance needs, or reproducibility constraints.\n41: \n42: ## Managing Dependencies\n43: \n44: Add a dependency:\n45: \n46: ```bash\n47: uv add <package-name>\n48: ```\n49: \n50: Add a development-only dependency group member by editing `pyproject.toml` and\n51: running:\n52: \n53: ```bash\n54: uv sync --group codegen --group testing\n55: ```\n56: \n57: When adding a new tool, prefer placing it in an existing dependency group if it\n58: belongs clearly to code generation or testing. Create a new group only when the\n59: tooling serves a separate workflow that would otherwise blur repository setup.\n60: \n61: ## Common Commands\n62: \n63: ### Structural Generation\n64: \n65: Run one target:\n66: \n67: ```bash\n68: uv run python -m cvn_codegen.xsdata_runner cvn\n69: uv run python -m cvn_codegen.xsdata_runner specification_manual\n70: uv run python -m cvn_codegen.xsdata_runner tree_model\n71: ```\n72: \n73: Run all structural targets:\n74: \n75: ```bash\n76: uv run python -m cvn_codegen.xsdata_runner all\n77: ```\n78: \n79: ### Tests\n80: \n81: ```bash\n82: uv run pytest tests\n83: uv run pytest tests/test_xsdata_runner_unit.py -v\n84: uv run pytest tests/test_xsdata_runner_smoke.py -v\n85: ```\n86: \n87: All automated tests should live under `tests/` so the local and CI entry point\n88: remains:\n89: \n90: ```bash\n91: uv run pytest tests\n92: ```\n93: \n94: ### Parse Smoke Checks\n95: \n96: Parse `SpecificationManual.xml`:\n97: \n98: ```bash\n99: uv run python - <<'PY'\n100: from pathlib import Path\n101: from xsdata_pydantic.bindings import XmlParser\n102: from generated.specification_manual import SpecificationManual\n103: \n104: parser = XmlParser()\n105: result = parser.from_path(\n106:     Path(\"docs/CvnXML_v1.4.3_2.1_17012025/XML/SpecificationManual.xml\"),\n107:     SpecificationManual,\n108: )\n109: print(type(result).__name__)\n110: PY\n111: ```\n112: \n113: Parse `CVNTreeModel.xml` only as a known-limitation check:\n114: \n115: ```bash\n116: uv run python - <<'PY'\n117: from pathlib import Path\n118: from xsdata_pydantic.bindings import XmlParser\n119: from generated.tree_model import CvntreeModel\n120: \n121: parser = XmlParser()\n122: result = parser.from_path(\n123:     Path(\"docs/CvnXML_v1.4.3_2.1_17012025/XML/CVNTreeModel.xml\"),\n124:     CvntreeModel,\n125: )\n126: print(type(result).__name__)\n127: PY\n128: ```\n129: \n130: This currently fails because the XML canonical file diverges from its XSD. See\n131: `docs/pipeline/known_limitations.md`.\n132: \n133: ### Generic Python Execution Patterns\n134: \n135: ```bash\n136: uv run python path/to/script.py\n137: uv run python -m package.module\n138: uv run --python 3.14 python path/to/script.py\n139: ```