7: planning record.\n48: \n49: The normalization retrofit described here has now been implemented.\n50: \n51: The implementation scope of this hotfix is intentionally narrow and must stay\n52: centered on normalization enrichment, not on structural-generation expansion or\n53: roadmap replanning already covered elsewhere.\n54: \n55: This hotfix does include:\n56: \n57: - additive enrichment of the normalization output from issue `#13`\n58: - machine-readable resolution of `ManualCodeEntry.manual_reference_table`\n59: - loading and indexing of canonical auxiliary XML sources needed for that\n60:   resolution\n61: - classification of serialization patterns from auxiliary technical metadata\n62: - classification of semantic reference kinds needed by later semantic work\n63: - explicit mismatch reporting for unresolved, ambiguous, subtype-missing, and\n64:   under-traced cases\n65: \n66: This hotfix does not include:\n67: \n68: - structural-generation target expansion already implemented through hotfix `#4`\n69: - roadmap replanning for issues `#14` to `#17` documented by hotfix `#6`\n70: - final semantic policy decisions such as open-versus-closed treatment\n71: - domain-model generation or rich domain normalization of auxiliary catalogs\n72: \n73: It converts the documentation knowledge established by hotfix `#3` into stable\n74: normalized metadata consumable by later issues.\n75: \n76: ## Issues Affected\n77: \n78: - issue `#13`\n79: \n80: ## Required Changes To Issue `#13`\n81: \n82: Issue `#13` should remain marked as completed for the core normalization layer,\n83: but its document and implementation plan must now be expanded to include an\n84: additive resolution layer over auxiliary references.\n85: \n86: ### Corrected Execution Objective\n87: \n88: The real objective of this hotfix is not only to keep\n89: `manual_reference_table` as a documented anchor, but to transform that anchor\n90: into executable normalization metadata so issue `#14` does not need to rebuild\n91: source-resolution logic from prose documents.\n92: \n93: This means the implementation must absorb the operational knowledge established\n94: by hotfix `#3` that was still only documented, while staying within the\n95: technical boundaries of issue `#13` and without duplicating hotfix `#4` or\n96: hotfix `#6`.\n97: \n98: ### Contract Changes Required\n99: \n100: The normalization contract in `src/cvn_codegen/normalization_types.py` must be\n101: extended with additive fields rather than by replacing the current structures.\n102: \n103: At minimum, the normalization output needs a typed representation for:\n104: \n105: 1. reference resolution status\n106: 2. resolved source family\n107: 3. resolved source artifact name\n108: 4. serialization pattern classification\n109: 5. semantic reference kind\n110: 6. subtype-backing flag or subtype metadata\n111: \n112: The preferred design is to keep `ManualCodeEntry` as the normalized extraction\n113: view of `SpecificationManual.xml` and to attach the richer auxiliary-reference\n114: resolution metadata to `NormalizedCodeEntry`, which is the repository-level\n115: aggregate consumed by later stages.\n116: \n117: The design must preserve backward compatibility for current consumers of:\n118: \n119: - `ManualCodeEntry`\n120: - `NormalizedCodeEntry`\n121: - `NormalizationResult`\n122: \n123: ### New Types Required\n124: \n125: Issue `#13` should add typed structures equivalent in intent to the following:\n126: \n127: - a reference-source enum or constrained type\n128: - a serialization-pattern enum or constrained type\n129: - a semantic-reference-kind enum or constrained type\n130: - a reference-resolution trace type when needed for artifact traceability\n131: - a reference-resolution record attached to normalized entries\n132: \n133: The exact names may vary, but the contract must support these categories:\n134: \n135: 1. direct `ReferenceTables` table\n136: 2. subtype-backed table\n137: 3. side-package registry\n138: 4. side-package thesaurus\n139: 5. hierarchical thematic table\n140: 6. unresolved manual-only reference\n141: 7. technically present but under-traced table\n142: \n143: At minimum, the implementation should support a record equivalent in intent to:\n144: \n145: 1. raw manual reference value\n146: 2. resolution status\n147: 3. resolved source family\n148: 4. resolved artifact name\n149: 5. resolved technical or logical source name\n150: 6. serialization pattern classification\n151: 7. semantic reference kind\n152: 8. subtype-backing indicator\n153: 9. subtype-support indicator or subtype metadata summary\n154: 10. traceability and diagnostics\n155: \n156: ### New Hand-Maintained Modules Required\n157: \n158: Issue `#13` currently spreads normalization across a small flat set of modules.\n159: For the hotfix implementation, that flat shape no longer needs to be preserved\n160: strictly.\n161: \n162: The preferred implementation is now a small dedicated subpackage under\n163: `src/cvn_codegen/` for auxiliary-source support and resolution.\n164: \n165: The following responsibilities must be added under `src/cvn_codegen/`:\n166: \n167: - loading and indexing of `ReferenceTables.xml`\n168: - loading and indexing of `Subtype_Spa.xml`\n169: - loading and indexing of `Entity.xml` for normalization-grade registry\n170:   traceability\n171: - loading and indexing of `Thesaurus*.xml` for normalization-grade vocabulary\n172:   traceability\n173: - resolution of `manual_reference_table` against those sources\n174: - classification of serialization patterns from machine-readable metadata\n175: - classification of semantic reference kinds from the resolved source family and\n176:   technical metadata\n177: \n178: The logic must stay outside `src/generated/`.\n179: \n180: The preferred module split is equivalent in intent to:\n181: \n182: - `auxiliary_sources/reference_tables_metadata.py`\n183: - `auxiliary_sources/subtypes_metadata.py`\n184: - `auxiliary_sources/entity_metadata.py`\n185: - `auxiliary_sources/thesaurus_metadata.py`\n186: - `auxiliary_sources/reference_resolution.py`\n187: \n188: Exact filenames may vary, but the separation of responsibilities should remain\n189: clear.\n190: \n191: ### Canonical Auxiliary Parse Scope Required\n192: \n193: To make hotfix `#5` fully absorb the actionable knowledge from hotfix `#3`, the\n194: implementation must parse the canonical auxiliary sources at least to the depth\n195: needed for deterministic normalization resolution.\n196: \n197: #### `ReferenceTables.xml`\n198: \n199: The implementation must parse and index at minimum:\n200: \n201: 1. table name\n202: 2. version\n203: 3. `antecesorTable`\n204: 4. `source`\n205: 5. `XMLDataType`\n206: 6. `XMLProperty`\n207: 7. `XMLIndicator`\n208: 8. item count\n209: 9. hierarchical-table signals such as item-level `AntecesorCode`\n210: 10. delegation signals such as item-level `Delegate`\n211: \n212: #### `Subtype_Spa.xml`\n213: \n214: The implementation must parse and index at minimum:\n215: \n216: 1. source item code\n217: 2. preferred name\n218: 3. `CodeSubtype1`\n219: 4. optional `CodeSubtype2`\n220: 5. whether second-level subtype support exists\n221: \n222: #### `Entity.xml`\n223: \n224: `Entity.xml` must now be parsed during hotfix `#5`, not deferred, but only to a\n225: normalization-grade depth.\n226: \n227: That means the implementation must at minimum:\n228: \n229: 1. verify successful parse of the canonical registry\n230: 2. expose stable artifact-level traceability for entity-backed references\n231: 3. build a minimal registry index or equivalent lookup support\n232: 4. preserve that `Entity` is a structured external registry, not a compact enum\n233: \n234: This hotfix does not require full semantic normalization of every entity record.\n235: \n236: #### `Thesaurus*.xml`\n237: \n238: The implementation must parse the canonical thesaurus family at least to the\n239: depth needed to classify thesaurus-backed references as hierarchical controlled\n240: vocabularies.\n241: \n242: The bilingual `Thesaurus.xml` should be treated as the primary canonical source\n243: unless a stronger implementation reason requires a different source-of-truth\n244: policy.\n245: \n246: At minimum, the implementation must preserve:\n247: \n248: 1. artifact traceability\n249: 2. hierarchical nature through `itemAncestorId`\n250: 3. multilingual nature\n251: 4. distinction from compact enum-like tables\n252: \n253: ### Orchestration Changes Required\n254: \n255: `build_normalization_result(...)` in `src/cvn_codegen/normalization.py` must be\n256: expanded so the final normalized result includes auxiliary-reference resolution.\n257: \n258: The corrected orchestration must:\n259: \n260: 1. keep the current code-overlap logic unchanged\n\n(Showing lines 1-260 of 598. Use offset=261 to continue.)\n</content>",
