            "output": "<path>/home/carlos/uni/tfg/TFG-open-cvn-schema/docs/roadmap/hotfixes/hotfix-6-roadmap-realignment-for-auxiliary-catalog-semantic-integration.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Hotfix 6 - Roadmap Realignment For Auxiliary Catalog Semantic Integration\n2: \n3: ## Summary\n4: \n5: Hotfix `#6` records the roadmap correction required after hotfixes `#4` and\n6: `#5`.\n7: \n8: The original roadmap for issues `#14` to `#17` assumed that the repository would\n9: reach semantic work after only two technical preparation stages:\n10: \n11: 1. structural bindings for the core schemas\n12: 2. normalization of `SpecificationManual.xml` and `CVNTreeModel.xml`\n13: \n14: After the auxiliary source-package analysis from hotfix `#3`, that sequencing is\n15: no longer sufficient. Future issues must explicitly incorporate the auxiliary\n16: catalog families recently added in the source bundle sent by FECYT and the\n17: resolution layer built over them.\n18: \n19: This hotfix does not implement those future issues. It documents exactly how the\n20: already created issue set must be replanned.\n21: \n22: ## Motivation\n23: \n24: If the roadmap is left unchanged:\n25: \n26: - issue `#14` would try to define semantic policy over incomplete normalized\n27:   inputs\n28: - issue `#15` would likely mix discovery work with generation work\n29: - issue `#16` would test a pipeline that still lacks the now-documented\n30:   auxiliary-source integration stage\n31: - issue `#17` would document an incomplete workflow\n32: \n33: ## Scope Of This Hotfix\n34: \n35: This hotfix is a planning and correction record.\n36: \n37: It does not itself:\n38: \n39: - implement issue `#14`\n40: - implement issue `#15`\n41: - implement issue `#16`\n42: - implement issue `#17`\n43: \n44: It defines the required replanning for those issues and for the roadmap-level\n45: documents that describe them.\n46: \n47: ## Issues Affected\n48: \n49: - issue `#8`\n50: - issue `#14`\n51: - issue